# Dependencies are never committed. `lib/` *is* committed, on purpose: see the
# `//scripts` note in package.json. pnpm decides a git-hosted package needs a
# build whenever a `prepare` script exists, then only runs prepublish/prepack/
# publish, so a source-only package either demands an SHA-pinned `allowBuilds`
# entry or installs with lib/ missing. Committing the artifact is what lets
# `dsh plugin add github:...` work with no manual step. Run `npm run build` and
# commit lib/ alongside any src/ change.
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Dependencies are installed with pnpm by the harness; an npm lockfile would be
# dead weight here and npm's own default .gitignore excludes it from libraries.
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml

*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
